What is it ?
~~~~~~~~~~~~
      This door was a quick solution to users downloading files from a KFB
      filebase without having to search the entire filebase if they already
      know what file they want.

      It will list the file area names, and they just have to enter the area
      and the name of the file they want

      OK, so it isn't the prettiest door you ever saw, but it does the job !
      (the door took me 30 minutes, these docs took longer !)


How do I set it up ?
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
      Make a directory called KFBraw in DOORS: and copy the program to it.

      If you already use my filelist generator for KFB, make a copy of the
      config file to this directory, renaming it as you go to 'kfbraw.cfg'

      Otherwise, make a note of all your FBxx areas used, and edit the
      example config in this archive.

              Line  1 is the file area description for FB01:
              Line  5 is  ""  ""  ""  ""  ""  ""  ""   FB05:
              Line 33 is  ""  ""  ""  ""  ""  ""  ""   FB33:

                               and so on...


      Put the descriptions of areas after the ';'s - DON'T DELETE THEM !

      Run the program as an ordinary door using function 34.

      If you don't like the colours, get a hex-editor out and change them !


      Non-KFB sysops could also potentially use this door if they want to
      make some assigns up - each file area needs an assign like this...

                  ASSIGN FB01: <path of individual file area>

      The FBxx *must* be from '01' to '99'

      That way, regardless of filebase system used, a user could 'raw dl'
      a file as long as it was assigned, and he knew the filename.


